    "created_at": "2016-04-15T16:14:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-15T16:14:46Z",
    "body": "Good point. My first thought after reading this issue was that we should try to be as consistent as possible with how drawImage() handles its sources: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#check-the-usability-of-the-image-argument\n\ndrawImage() would just fail silently in this case, which is not an option with createImageBitmap: the promise must be either resolved or rejected.  Since zero-size ImageBitmap objects are not allowed to exist (the object must have bitmap data), rejection is the logical option.\n\nIn the case where a crop rectangle is specified, it may make sense to return a transparent black bitmap the size of the crop rect instead of throwing an exception.  Any opinions on that?\n",
